# Template drift allowlist for zudo-design-token-lint (doc site).
# Generated projects start from create-zudo-doc templates; this file lists
# intentional divergences so `pnpm check:template-drift` exits 0.
#
# Format: one repo-relative path per line (no leading slash).
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
#
# Re-baselined against create-zudo-doc 11.0.0 (the version pinned in
# doc/package.json's devDependencies) for the zudo-doc 10→11 bump (issue
# #205); the entries below date from the zudo-doc 6→10 / zfb 4→6 port (issue
# #197) and still hold, because 11.0.0's templates/base and
# templates/features/i18n are byte-identical to 10.0.3. tsconfig.json matches
# the template byte-for-byte, so it needs no entry. The drift check
# (scripts/check-template-drift.sh) only walks
# node_modules/create-zudo-doc/templates/{base,features}; top-level identity
# files (zfb.config.ts, wrangler.toml, package.json, setup-preset.json) have
# no template counterpart there and are never compared.

# Customized for the hybrid layout: resolves the project name from the ROOT
# package.json and reads/writes the repo-root `.claude/skills/` (not doc/.claude).
scripts/setup-doc-skill.sh

# Template stub + the docHistory feature's DocHistoryBoundary patch, but with a
# STATIC import of src/chrome-bindings instead of the virtual module, so zfb's
# island scanner reaches the <Playground> island (in-file comment explains).
pages/docs/[[...slug]].tsx
pages/[locale]/docs/[[...slug]].tsx

# Template CSS entry + the designTokenPanel zdtp import, plus project brand
# typography overrides (Futura tokens / [data-header-logo]); see in-file comments.
src/styles/global.css

# Branded favicon assets instead of the generic ones; the SVG template is absent
# because the detailed source mark is unreadable at favicon sizes.
public/favicon-16x16.png
public/favicon-32x32.png
public/favicon.ico
public/favicon.svg

# Stricter versioned-route and allowlist behavior than the scaffolded checker.
scripts/check-links.js
